.nh
.TH "PB-WAIT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-wait - Wait for a machine readiness condition


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb wait <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Wait until a machine satisfies a readiness condition chosen with --for. runtime waits for an
eligible runtime that is ready or degraded. transport (the default) also probes an authenticated
connection to the machine. ssh also waits for managed SSH to be ready. --timeout bounds the wait
(up to 24h); mere connectivity is never treated as readiness.

.PP
Exit status: 0 ready, 203 timed out, 205 cancelled, 1 any other failure.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--for\fP="transport"
	readiness condition: runtime, transport, or ssh

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for wait

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=5m0s
	maximum time to wait


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb wait studio
  pb wait studio --for ssh --timeout 10m
  pb wait studio --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
